Admittedly having only ascended once, I found the "oLS pretty useless
because by the time I hit the upper planes I was so badass that I
didn't need it (AC: -40 with #twoweapon, HP: 335). But there were
definitely situations where it would have come in handy (for example
if I had tried to carry a c corpse around - I was too scared of
fucking up the ascension and I had /oD charges left, I'm sure I would
have jumped into a pit by mistake at least once - so I didn't). But at
that point "oESP would have been pretty useless as well because I was
blind most of the time anyway on the ascension run because I had
mapped Gehennom well and h was genocided.

JMHO, I think "oLS is better if you are prone to making stupid
mistakes like tripping with a c corpse or accidentally bumping into a
floating eye at low level, etc. "oESP is better if you have a weak
character for some reason and are exceptionally good at the game (i.e.
going for conducts or speed or something) where you won't make that
kind of mistake but can make full use of the extra information
provided.

Also, IMO, "oESP is a lot less useful if you have warning, as telling
the difference between a Minotaur and an Arch-Lich is probably not
*that* important if you need to run from both.

